# [AGENTPROTO](../wg/agentproto.html)

## Summary

The AGENTPROTO working group held its initial session at IETF 127. The session was chaired by Orie Steele and Leslie Daigle, with Area Directors Zaheduzzaman Sarker and Andrew Newton in attendance.

The meeting covered working group administration and operational procedures, followed by technical presentations and discussions on agentic AI use cases, requirements, and architectural frameworks. Primary technical topics included the distinction between Agentproto and existing protocols (e.g., A2A, MCP), the definition of dialogues versus tasks, multi-hop propagation strategies (minimal vs. full chains), and two-party versus multi-party interaction models.

---

## Key Discussion Points

### Working Group Administration and Operational Mode
*Presentation: [Chair slides](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-agentproto-chair-slides-01)*  
*Presenter: Orie Steele*

* **GitHub vs. Mailing List Workflow**: The chairs outlined the working group's operational model. Editors may use GitHub to rapidly iterate on draft revisions and manage issue tracking. However, substantive technical discussions, summaries of closed issues, and consensus calls must be brought to and confirmed on the main IETF mailing list (noted by Leonel Mora, Eric Rescorla, Zaheduzzaman Sarker, and Leslie Daigle).
* **Virtual Interim Meetings**: Broad support was expressed by participants (including Jonathan Rosenberg, Thomas Hardjono, Hesham Moussa, Cullen Jennings, Antoine Fressancourt, Zaheduzzaman Sarker, and Mark Nottingham) for holding frequent virtual interim meetings (e.g., bi-weekly) to maintain working group momentum between IETF plenaries.

